accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  corrected type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  02 removed_month 94 accessioned on  02 removed_month 94 at 13 10 clinical data  none provided                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  right   biopsy  infiltrating ductal carcinoma  poorly differentiated  85    and intraductal carcinoma  15    see note  note  tumor involvement measures 1 3cm in greatest dimension based on slide section  inked resection margins are positive for infiltrating carcinoma  the frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  diagnosis by  g  richard dickersin  m d  signed on  07 removed_month 94 at 16 44                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  right   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors